note aien-supervise-root: the only part of aien-supervise that runs as root. Invoked through one
note sudoers rule as `aien-supervise-root VERB NAME`, VERB run|stop|kill|check. It reads only
note /etc/aien-supervise/services/NAME.svc, refuses unless that file, its directories and every
note program and file it hands on are root-owned and not group/other-writable, and never runs a
note service as root: it builds the per-service sandbox and execs
note   [nice] -> setpriv (uid/gid/groups, no_new_privs, empty bounding/inheritable/ambient caps)
note   -> bwrap (user, pid, ipc, uts, cgroup namespaces; optional net; read-only /usr and /etc,
note      declared binds, own /proc, minimal /dev, private /tmp; seccomp allowlist) -> program
note after putting itself into /sys/fs/cgroup/aien-supervise/NAME (memory.max, cpu.max, pids.max)
note and loading the service's nftables table (meta skuid). Exit 2 = refused; nothing ran.
text tsdir "/etc/aien-supervise/services/"
text tbwrap "/usr/bin/bwrap"
